#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Prove the publish tokens can publish every Core or Meta package, publishing nothing.

Meta 0.9.9's promote published the GitHub release and PyPI, then npm refused
`@rkat/meta-sdk` (404 on the PUT: the token's package list lacked it) and the
release split. A token-scope, expiry or revocation problem must show before
any publication instead. This script asks each registry the one question that
proves a token's publish right without a write: it re-sends the already
published artifact of an already published version, so the registry first
authorizes the write and then refuses it as a duplicate.

    release-registry-preflight --product core|meta
        [--mode plan|probe]          default plan: read and print, write nothing
        [--registry npm,pypi,crates] default: all three
        [--crates family|all]        default family: the fixed crates.io sample
        [--release-version X]        never probed (besides the manifests' versions)
        [--report FILE]              JSON report

Package names come from the repository, never from a hand list: Core's crates
from the script ci/products.json names (scripts/release-rust-crates.sh), Meta's
from its publish_order there; the PyPI and npm names from the SDK manifests.

Safety rules, each enforced here and covered by scripts/test_release_registry_preflight.py:

(a) Only an already published version is probed, never the version about to
    be released: the probe version is the newest final version the registry
    lists that is not the release version (--release-version and every
    manifest version of the product). Before any probe the registry must list
    it, its artifact is downloaded anonymously and must match the registry's
    own digest (npm sha512 integrity, PyPI sha256, crates.io checksum), and
    its own manifest must name the package and that version. A package with
    nothing to probe fails; nothing is sent for it.
(b) The default mode is `plan`: every anonymous read and check of (a), and the
    request each probe would send, but no write and no token read.
(c) crates.io takes one token of the account's publish-update rate limit
    (burst 30, one more a minute) for each probe, even a refused one, before
    its duplicate check. `family` (the default, and the release-time gate)
    probes a fixed sample, FAMILY_SAMPLE, and checks every other crate of the
    product anonymously: it exists, is not trusted-publishing-only, and its
    owners include every owner of the probed crates. `all` probes every crate,
    paced (--crates-burst at most 30 back to back, then one per
    --crates-interval of at least 60 seconds), and is refused inside a
    release workflow: it is the early registry-preflight.yml dispatch only.
(d) Every package of the product gets a row: PASS, FAIL, INCONCLUSIVE or SKIP
    (plan mode, or a crate outside the family sample), the registry's HTTP
    status and its exact answer, in the log, the JSON report and the job
    summary. No token or token-derived value is ever printed or written:
    every captured answer is redacted before use.

Each probe is preceded by a control: the same request without valid
credentials. If the registry gives the control the duplicate answer as well,
that answer does not depend on the token and proves nothing: INCONCLUSIVE.

npm:    GET /-/whoami with the token (an invalid, expired or revoked token
        fails here), then PUT the publish document `npm publish` would send
        for the existing version, under the dist-tag `registry-preflight`.
        403 "cannot publish over the previously published versions": PASS.
        401, 403 (any other), 404 (npm's answer to a write the token may not
        make, the 0.9.9 refusal): FAIL. 2xx: FAIL (incident). The PUT is sent
        directly, not through the npm CLI: npm 11 refuses an existing version
        before it sends anything, in the registry's own words.
PyPI:   `twine upload` (no --skip-existing) of the exact published wheel.
        Exit 0 (HTTP 200: Warehouse answers an exact duplicate with 200 and
        writes nothing, after its upload-permission check): PASS. 401 or 403:
        FAIL. 400 "File already exists" (the bytes differ, which (a)
        excludes): INCONCLUSIVE.
crates: PUT /api/v1/crates/new with the exact published .crate and its name
        and version. 400 "crate version `V` is already uploaded" (the check
        inside the publish transaction, after the token, scope, trusted
        publishing and owner checks; the transaction rolls back): PASS. 401
        or 403: FAIL. 429: wait for the advertised time and retry once. Any
        other 400 (body validation runs before the token check): INCONCLUSIVE.
        A crate missing from crates.io fails: a first publication needs the
        publish-new scope, which no probe can prove without publishing.

Every INCONCLUSIVE answer is retried once, then fails closed. Exit 0 only when
no package is FAIL or INCONCLUSIVE, and in probe mode at least one passed.
Exit 2 for a usage or repository error, before any request.

Tokens: NPM_TOKEN, PYPI_API_TOKEN, CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN, read in probe mode
only, for the selected registries only. They go only to the real registries
over https, or to a loopback stub named by MEERKAT_REGISTRY_PREFLIGHT_STUB
(the self-test), and never in a redirect.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import base64
import dataclasses
import email.parser
import email.utils
import hashlib
import io
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import tarfile
import tempfile
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
import zipfile
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any, Callable

if sys.version_info < (3, 11):
    sys.exit("release-registry-preflight needs Python >= 3.11 (tomllib)")

import tomllib  # noqa: E402

REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
USER_AGENT = "meerkat-registry-preflight (release tooling)"
PROBE_DIST_TAG = "registry-preflight"
# Sent by the control upload instead of a token: not a token of any account.
CONTROL_PASSWORD = "registry-preflight-control-not-a-token"
REGISTRIES = ("npm", "pypi", "crates")
TOKEN_ENV = {"npm": "NPM_TOKEN", "pypi": "PYPI_API_TOKEN", "crates": "CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN"}
STUB_ENV = "MEERKAT_REGISTRY_PREFLIGHT_STUB"
# Credentials twine must never see (it would try trusted publishing with an
# OIDC request token).
UNSHARED_ENV = (
    "NODE_AUTH_TOKEN",
    "GH_TOKEN",
    "GITHUB_TOKEN",
    "ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_TOKEN",
    "ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_URL",
)
# A run inside these workflows is a release-time check: never the full probe.
RELEASE_WORKFLOWS = re.compile(r"/\.github/workflows/(release|meta-release)\.ya?ml@")
# crates.io publish-update bucket: burst 30, one token a minute
# (crates.io src/rate_limiter.rs).
CRATES_BURST_LIMIT = 30
CRATES_MIN_INTERVAL = 60
# Longest wait for an advertised Retry-After before the retry.
MAX_RETRY_AFTER = 900
FINAL_VERSION = re.compile(r"^\d+(?:\.\d+)+$")
MAX_ANSWER = 600


@dataclasses.dataclass(frozen=True)
class ProductSpec:
    npm_manifests: tuple[str, ...]
    pypi_manifests: tuple[str, ...]
    # One crate per crates.io crate-scope name family (a token's crate
    # scope names a crate or a `prefix*` pattern).
    family_sample: tuple[str, ...]


PRODUCTS = {
    "core": ProductSpec(
        npm_manifests=("sdks/typescript/package.json", "sdks/web/package.json"),
        pypi_manifests=("sdks/python/pyproject.toml",),
        family_sample=("meerkat-core", "rkat"),
    ),
    "meta": ProductSpec(
        npm_manifests=("meta/sdk/typescript/package.json",),
        pypi_manifests=("meta/sdk/python/pyproject.toml",),
        family_sample=("meta-extension-state", "meerkat-meta"),
    ),
}

PASS, FAIL, INCONCLUSIVE, SKIP = "PASS", "FAIL", "INCONCLUSIVE", "SKIP"


class UsageError(Exception):
    """A usage or repository error: exit 2 before any request."""


@dataclasses.dataclass
class Product:
    name: str
    crates: list[str]
    pypi: list[str]
    npm: list[str]
    excluded_versions: set[str]
    family_sample: tuple[str, ...]


@dataclasses.dataclass
class Row:
    registry: str
    package: str
    verdict: str
    version: str | None = None
    status: int | None = None
    answer: str = ""
    detail: str = ""
    control: dict[str, Any] | None = None
    artifact: dict[str, Any] | None = None


@dataclasses.dataclass
class Response:
    status: int | None
    headers: dict[str, str]
    body: bytes
    error: str | None = None


@dataclasses.dataclass
class Endpoints:
    npm: str
    pypi_index: str
    pypi_upload: str
    crates_api: str
    crates_static: str
    stub: bool


class Secrets:
    """Every secret value and token-derived form, for redaction."""

    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self.values: list[str] = []

    def add(self, value: str) -> None:
        if value and value not in self.values:
            self.values.append(value)
            self.values.sort(key=len, reverse=True)

    def redact(self, text: str) -> str:
        for value in self.values:
            text = text.replace(value, "***")
        return text


class NoRedirect(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):
    """A request carrying credentials never follows a redirect."""

    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):  # noqa: D401
        return None


PLAIN_OPENER = urllib.request.build_opener()
CREDENTIAL_OPENER = urllib.request.build_opener(NoRedirect())


def http(
    method: str,
    url: str,
    *,
    headers: dict[str, str] | None = None,
    body: bytes | None = None,
    credentials: bool = False,
    timeout: float = 120.0,
) -> Response:
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        url, data=body, method=method, headers={"User-Agent": USER_AGENT, **(headers or {})}
    )
    opener = CREDENTIAL_OPENER if credentials else PLAIN_OPENER
    try:
        with opener.open(request, timeout=timeout) as response:
            return Response(response.status, _lower(response.headers), response.read())
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:
        try:
            payload = error.read()
        except OSError:
            payload = b""
        return Response(error.code, _lower(error.headers), payload)
    except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError, OSError, ValueError) as error:
        return Response(None, {}, b"", error=f"{type(error).__name__}: {error}")


def _lower(headers: Any) -> dict[str, str]:
    return {key.lower(): value for key, value in (headers.items() if headers else [])}


def _transient(response: Response) -> bool:
    return response.status is None or response.status == 429 or response.status >= 500


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository: package names and the versions never probed.


def _toml(path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:
    try:
        with path.open("rb") as handle:
            return tomllib.load(handle)
    except (OSError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError) as error:
        raise UsageError(f"cannot read {path}: {error}") from error


def _json(path: Path) -> Any:
    try:
        return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:
        raise UsageError(f"cannot read {path}: {error}") from error


def _crate_list(repo: Path, product: str) -> list[str]:
    products = _json(repo / "ci" / "products.json").get("products")
    entry = next((item for item in products or [] if item.get("name") == product), None)
    if entry is None:
        raise UsageError(f"ci/products.json has no product {product!r}")
    order = entry.get("publish_order")
    if isinstance(order, str):
        # The canonical list script (Core: scripts/release-rust-crates.sh).
        script = (repo / order).resolve()
        if not script.is_file() or repo.resolve() not in script.parents:
            raise UsageError(f"{product}'s publish_order names {order!r}, not a script in the repository")
        result = subprocess.run(
            ["bash", str(script)],
            cwd=repo,
            env={"PATH": os.environ.get("PATH", "/usr/bin:/bin"), "LC_ALL": "C"},
            capture_output=True,
            text=True,
            check=False,
            timeout=60,
        )
        if result.returncode != 0:
            raise UsageError(f"{order} failed ({result.returncode}): {result.stderr.strip()}")
        names = [line.strip() for line in result.stdout.splitlines() if line.strip()]
    elif isinstance(order, list):
        names = [str(name) for name in order]
    else:
        raise UsageError(f"ci/products.json: {product} has no publish_order")
    bad = [name for name in names if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_-]+", name)]
    if not names or bad or len(set(names)) != len(names):
        raise UsageError(f"{product}'s crate list is empty, malformed or repeats a crate: {names}")
    return names


def _product_versions(repo: Path, product: str, crates: list[str]) -> set[str]:
    versions: set[str] = set()
    if product == "core":
        version = _toml(repo / "Cargo.toml").get("workspace", {}).get("package", {}).get("version")
        if isinstance(version, str):
            versions.add(version)
    else:
        for crate in crates:
            manifest = repo / "meta" / "crates" / crate / "Cargo.toml"
            if manifest.is_file():
                version = _toml(manifest).get("package", {}).get("version")
                if isinstance(version, str):
                    versions.add(version)
    if not versions:
        raise UsageError(f"cannot read {product}'s release version from the repository")
    return versions


def load_product(repo: Path, product: str, release_version: str | None) -> Product:
    spec = PRODUCTS[product]
    crates = _crate_list(repo, product)
    excluded = _product_versions(repo, product, crates)
    pypi: list[str] = []
    for relative in spec.pypi_manifests:
        project = _toml(repo / relative).get("project", {})
        if not isinstance(project.get("name"), str):
            raise UsageError(f"{relative} has no [project] name")
        pypi.append(project["name"])
        if isinstance(project.get("version"), str):
            excluded.add(project["version"])
    npm: list[str] = []
    for relative in spec.npm_manifests:
        manifest = _json(repo / relative)
        if not isinstance(manifest, dict) or not isinstance(manifest.get("name"), str):
            raise UsageError(f"{relative} has no package name")
        if manifest.get("private"):
            raise UsageError(f"{relative} is private: it publishes nothing")
        npm.append(manifest["name"])
        if isinstance(manifest.get("version"), str):
            excluded.add(manifest["version"])
    if release_version:
        excluded.add(release_version.removeprefix("v"))
    return Product(product, crates, pypi, npm, excluded, spec.family_sample)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Versions and artifacts.


def version_key(version: str) -> tuple[int, ...] | None:
    """Sort key of a final release version; None for anything else."""
    if not FINAL_VERSION.match(version):
        return None
    return tuple(int(part) for part in version.split("."))


def choose_version(published: list[str], excluded: set[str]) -> str | None:
    """The newest published final version that is not about to be released."""
    finals = [v for v in published if version_key(v) is not None and v not in excluded]
    return max(finals, key=version_key) if finals else None


def no_version_detail(published: list[str], excluded: set[str]) -> str:
    if not published:
        return "the registry lists no published version: a first publication cannot be probed"
    return (
        "no published final version other than the release version "
        f"({', '.join(sorted(excluded))}) to probe; nothing was sent"
    )


def _sri_sha512(payload: bytes) -> str:
    return "sha512-" + base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha512(payload).digest()).decode("ascii")


def _tar_member(payload: bytes, name: str) -> bytes | None:
    try:
        with tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(payload), mode="r:gz") as archive:
            for member in archive.getmembers():
                if member.name == name and member.isfile():
                    handle = archive.extractfile(member)
                    return handle.read() if handle else None
    except (tarfile.TarError, OSError, EOFError):
        return None
    return None


def _normalize_project(name: str) -> str:
    return re.sub(r"[-_.]+", "-", name).lower()


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Answers and verdicts (pure, unit-tested row by row).


def _text(body: bytes) -> str:
    return body.decode("utf-8", errors="replace")


def npm_answer(response: Response) -> str:
    if response.status is None:
        return response.error or "no response"
    text = _text(response.body)
    try:
        document = json.loads(text)
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        return text.strip()
    if isinstance(document, dict):
        for key in ("error", "message", "reason"):
            if isinstance(document.get(key), str):
                return document[key]
    return text.strip()


def crates_answer(response: Response) -> str:
    if response.status is None:
        return response.error or "no response"
    text = _text(response.body)
    try:
        document = json.loads(text)
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        return text.strip()
    errors = document.get("errors") if isinstance(document, dict) else None
    if isinstance(errors, list):
        details = [str(item.get("detail")) for item in errors if isinstance(item, dict)]
        if details:
            return "; ".join(details)
    return text.strip()


NPM_DUPLICATE = re.compile(r"cannot publish over (?:the )?previously published version", re.IGNORECASE)


def npm_is_duplicate(response: Response) -> bool:
    return response.status == 403 and bool(NPM_DUPLICATE.search(npm_answer(response)))


def classify_npm(response: Response) -> tuple[str, str]:
    status = response.status
    if status is None:
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "no answer from the registry (network error)"
    if npm_is_duplicate(response):
        return PASS, "the registry authorized the token for this package, then refused the existing version"
    if 200 <= status < 300:
        return FAIL, "INCIDENT: the registry accepted a write of an already published version; stop and read the registry"
    if status == 401:
        if "otp" in response.headers.get("www-authenticate", "").lower() or re.search(
            r"one-time pass", npm_answer(response), re.IGNORECASE
        ):
            return FAIL, "the registry asks for a one-time password: the token cannot publish without 2FA bypass"
        return FAIL, "the registry refused the token: invalid, expired or revoked"
    if status == 404:
        return FAIL, (
            "the token may not publish this package: npm answers 404 to a write the token may not make "
            "(a granular token whose package list lacks it; the 0.9.9 refusal)"
        )
    if status == 403:
        return FAIL, "the registry refused the token for this package (permission, or 2FA required)"
    if status == 429 or status >= 500:
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "transient registry answer"
    return INCONCLUSIVE, "unexpected answer: it proves neither the publish right nor its absence"


def crates_is_duplicate(response: Response, version: str) -> bool:
    return response.status == 400 and bool(
        re.search(rf"crate version `{re.escape(version)}` is already uploaded", crates_answer(response))
    )


def classify_crates(response: Response, version: str) -> tuple[str, str]:
    status = response.status
    if status is None:
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "no answer from the registry (network error)"
    if crates_is_duplicate(response, version):
        return PASS, (
            "crates.io accepted the token (endpoint scope, crate scope, trusted publishing, ownership), "
            "then refused the existing version inside its publish transaction"
        )
    if 200 <= status < 300:
        return FAIL, "INCIDENT: crates.io accepted a publish of an already published version; stop and read the registry"
    if status in (401, 403):
        return FAIL, "crates.io refused the token for this crate (token, scope, ownership or trusted-publishing-only)"
    if status == 429:
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "rate limited before the token was proven"
    if status == 400:
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "crates.io refused the probe body before the version check: it proves nothing; fix the probe body"
    if status >= 500:
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "transient registry answer"
    return INCONCLUSIVE, "unexpected answer: it proves neither the publish right nor its absence"


TWINE_HTTP_ERROR = re.compile(r"HTTPError:\s*(\d{3})\b[^\n]*?\bfrom\s+(\S+)\s*\n?\s*([^\n]*)")
TWINE_RESPONSE = re.compile(r"Response from \S+\s+(\d{3})\b([^\n]*)")


@dataclasses.dataclass
class TwineResult:
    returncode: int | None
    output: str
    error: str | None = None


def twine_status(result: TwineResult) -> int | None:
    match = TWINE_HTTP_ERROR.search(result.output)
    if match:
        return int(match.group(1))
    match = TWINE_RESPONSE.search(result.output)
    return int(match.group(1)) if match else None


def twine_answer(result: TwineResult) -> str:
    if result.error:
        return result.error
    match = TWINE_HTTP_ERROR.search(result.output)
    if match:
        return f"HTTPError: {match.group(1)} from {match.group(2)}: {match.group(3).strip()}".rstrip(": ")
    match = TWINE_RESPONSE.search(result.output)
    if match:
        return f"{match.group(1)}{match.group(2)}".strip()
    lines = [line.strip() for line in result.output.splitlines() if line.strip()]
    return " | ".join(lines[-4:])


def classify_twine(result: TwineResult) -> tuple[str, str]:
    if result.returncode is None:
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "twine did not finish"
    if result.returncode == 0:
        return PASS, "PyPI checked the token's upload permission, then answered the exact duplicate with 200 and wrote nothing"
    status = twine_status(result)
    if status in (401, 403):
        return FAIL, "PyPI refused the token for this project"
    if status == 400 and re.search(r"file already exists", result.output, re.IGNORECASE):
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "PyPI holds a file of this name with other bytes; investigate before relying on the token"
    if status is not None and (status == 429 or status >= 500):
        return INCONCLUSIVE, "transient registry answer"
    return INCONCLUSIVE, "unexpected answer: it proves neither the upload right nor its absence"


def retry_after_seconds(response: Response, default: float) -> float:
    value = response.headers.get("retry-after", "").strip()
    if not value:
        return default
    if value.isdigit():
        return min(float(value), MAX_RETRY_AFTER)
    try:
        when = email.utils.parsedate_to_datetime(value)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return default
    if when.tzinfo is None:
        when = when.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)
    delta = (when - datetime.now(timezone.utc)).total_seconds() + 1.0
    return min(max(delta, 0.0), MAX_RETRY_AFTER)


def probe_delays(count: int, burst: int, interval: float) -> list[float]:
    """Seconds to wait before each crates.io probe: `burst` back to back, then one per interval."""
    return [0.0 if index < burst else float(interval) for index in range(count)]


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The run.


class Run:
    def __init__(self, args: argparse.Namespace, endpoints: Endpoints, product: Product) -> None:
        self.args = args
        self.endpoints = endpoints
        self.product = product
        self.probe = args.mode == "probe"
        self.secrets = Secrets()
        self.tokens: dict[str, str] = {}
        self.read_pace = 0.0 if endpoints.stub else 1.0
        self._last_api_read = 0.0
        if self.probe:
            for registry in args.registries:
                token = os.environ.get(TOKEN_ENV[registry], "").strip()
                self.tokens[registry] = token
                self.secrets.add(token)
                if token and registry == "pypi":
                    self.secrets.add(base64.b64encode(f"__token__:{token}".encode()).decode("ascii"))

    # ---- helpers

    def say(self, message: str) -> None:
        print(self.secrets.redact(message), flush=True)

    def clip(self, text: str) -> str:
        text = self.secrets.redact(" ".join(text.split()))
        return text if len(text) <= MAX_ANSWER else text[: MAX_ANSWER - 3] + "..."

    def sleep(self, seconds: float) -> None:
        if seconds > 0:
            time.sleep(seconds)

    def retried(self, send: Callable[[], Response]) -> Response:
        """Send; on a transient answer wait and send once more."""
        response = send()
        if not _transient(response):
            return response
        self.sleep(retry_after_seconds(response, self.args.retry_delay) if response.status == 429 else self.args.retry_delay)
        return send()

    def read(self, url: str, *, accept: str = "application/json", paced: bool = False) -> Response:
        """An anonymous read, retried once on a transient answer."""

        def send() -> Response:
            if paced and self.read_pace:
                self.sleep(self._last_api_read + self.read_pace - time.monotonic())
                self._last_api_read = time.monotonic()
            return http("GET", url, headers={"Accept": accept})

        return self.retried(send)

    def read_failure(self, registry: str, package: str, what: str, response: Response, version: str | None = None) -> Row:
        verdict = INCONCLUSIVE if _transient(response) else FAIL
        answer = {"npm": npm_answer, "crates": crates_answer}.get(
            registry, lambda read: _text(read.body) if read.status else (read.error or "")
        )(response)
        detail = f"cannot read {what}"
        if response.status == 404:
            detail = f"{what}: not found on the registry; a first publication cannot be probed"
        return Row(
            registry,
            package,
            verdict,
            version=version,
            status=response.status,
            answer=self.clip(answer),
            detail=detail,
        )

    def missing_token(self, registry: str, package: str) -> Row | None:
        if self.probe and not self.tokens.get(registry):
            return Row(registry, package, FAIL, detail=f"the {TOKEN_ENV[registry]} secret is empty or unset in this job")
        return None

    def attempt(self, send: Callable[[], Response], classify: Callable[[Response], tuple[str, str]]) -> tuple[Response, str, str]:
        """Send once; on an INCONCLUSIVE answer wait and send once more."""
        response = send()
        verdict, detail = classify(response)
        if verdict != INCONCLUSIVE:
            return response, verdict, detail
        wait = retry_after_seconds(response, 61.0) if response.status == 429 else self.args.retry_delay
        self.say(f"  inconclusive answer (HTTP {response.status}); one retry in {wait:.0f}s")
        self.sleep(wait)
        response = send()
        verdict, detail = classify(response)
        return response, verdict, detail

    def control_row(
        self,
        registry: str,
        package: str,
        version: str,
        control: Response,
        is_duplicate: bool,
        answer: str,
        artifact: dict[str, Any],
    ) -> Row | None:
        """A control answer that already looks like a pass makes any answer worthless."""
        record = {"status": control.status, "answer": self.clip(answer)}
        if is_duplicate:
            return Row(
                registry, package, INCONCLUSIVE, version=version, status=control.status, answer=self.clip(answer),
                detail="the registry gives the duplicate answer without valid credentials too: the answer does not depend on the token and proves nothing; the token was not sent",
                control=record, artifact=artifact,
            )
        if control.status is not None and 200 <= control.status < 300:
            return Row(
                registry, package, FAIL, version=version, status=control.status, answer=self.clip(answer),
                detail="INCIDENT: the registry accepted a write without valid credentials; stop and read the registry",
                control=record, artifact=artifact,
            )
        if control.status is None or control.status == 429 or control.status >= 500:
            return Row(
                registry, package, INCONCLUSIVE, version=version, status=control.status, answer=self.clip(answer),
                detail="the control request got no usable answer, so a later answer could not be told apart from one that ignores credentials; the token was not sent",
                control=record, artifact=artifact,
            )
        return None

    # ---- npm

    def npm_rows(self) -> list[Row]:
        names = self.product.npm
        missing = [row for row in (self.missing_token("npm", name) for name in names) if row]
        if missing:
            return missing
        if self.probe:
            token = self.tokens["npm"]
            whoami = self.retried(lambda: http(
                "GET", f"{self.endpoints.npm}/-/whoami",
                headers={"Accept": "application/json", "Authorization": f"Bearer {token}"}, credentials=True,
            ))
            if whoami.status != 200:
                refused = whoami.status in (401, 403)
                detail = (
                    "npm whoami refused the token (invalid, expired or revoked); no publish probe was sent"
                    if refused
                    else "npm whoami did not answer 200; no publish probe was sent"
                )
                return [
                    Row("npm", name, FAIL if refused else INCONCLUSIVE, status=whoami.status,
                        answer=self.clip(npm_answer(whoami)), detail=detail)
                    for name in names
                ]
            self.say("npm: the token authenticates (whoami 200; the account name is not printed)")
        return [self.npm_package(name) for name in names]

    def npm_package(self, name: str) -> Row:
        escaped = urllib.parse.quote(name, safe="@").replace("%2F", "%2f")
        url = f"{self.endpoints.npm}/{escaped}"
        packument = self.read(url, accept="application/vnd.npm.install-v1+json; q=1.0, application/json; q=0.8")
        if packument.status != 200:
            return self.read_failure("npm", name, f"the npm metadata of {name}", packument)
        try:
            document = json.loads(packument.body)
            versions = document["versions"]
            assert isinstance(versions, dict)
        except (ValueError, KeyError, AssertionError, TypeError):
            return Row("npm", name, FAIL, status=200, detail="the registry metadata has no versions object")
        version = choose_version(list(versions), self.product.excluded_versions)
        if version is None:
            return Row("npm", name, FAIL, detail=no_version_detail(list(versions), self.product.excluded_versions))
        dist = versions[version].get("dist") if isinstance(versions[version], dict) else None
        integrity = dist.get("integrity") if isinstance(dist, dict) else None
        tarball_url = dist.get("tarball") if isinstance(dist, dict) else None
        if not isinstance(integrity, str) or not integrity.startswith("sha512-") or not isinstance(tarball_url, str):
            return Row("npm", name, FAIL, version=version, detail="the registry records no sha512 integrity or tarball for this version")
        download = self.read(tarball_url, accept="application/octet-stream")
        if download.status != 200:
            return self.read_failure("npm", name, f"the {name} {version} tarball", download, version)
        tarball = download.body
        artifact = {"url": tarball_url, "digest": integrity, "verified": False}
        if _sri_sha512(tarball) not in integrity.split():
            return Row("npm", name, FAIL, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail="the downloaded tarball does not match the registry's sha512 integrity; nothing was sent")
        manifest_bytes = _tar_member(tarball, "package/package.json")
        try:
            manifest = json.loads(manifest_bytes or b"")
        except ValueError:
            manifest = None
        if not isinstance(manifest, dict) or manifest.get("name") != name or manifest.get("version") != version:
            return Row("npm", name, FAIL, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail="the tarball's package.json does not name this package and version; nothing was sent")
        artifact["verified"] = True
        body = json.dumps(self.npm_document(name, version, tarball, manifest)).encode()
        request = f"PUT {url} (the existing version, dist-tag {PROBE_DIST_TAG})"
        if not self.probe:
            return Row("npm", name, SKIP, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail=f"plan: would send {request}; published, sha512 verified")
        headers = {"Content-Type": "application/json", "Accept": "application/json", "npm-command": "publish"}
        control = http("PUT", url, headers=headers, body=body, credentials=True)
        blocked = self.control_row("npm", name, version, control, npm_is_duplicate(control), npm_answer(control), artifact)
        if blocked:
            return blocked
        token = self.tokens["npm"]
        response, verdict, detail = self.attempt(
            lambda: http("PUT", url, headers={**headers, "Authorization": f"Bearer {token}"}, body=body, credentials=True),
            classify_npm,
        )
        return Row("npm", name, verdict, version=version, status=response.status, answer=self.clip(npm_answer(response)),
                   detail=detail, control={"status": control.status, "answer": self.clip(npm_answer(control))}, artifact=artifact)

    def npm_document(self, name: str, version: str, tarball: bytes, manifest: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
        """The publish document libnpmpublish builds (npm 10, workspaces/libnpmpublish/lib/publish.js)."""
        manifest = dict(manifest)
        tarball_name = f"{name}-{version}.tgz"
        manifest["_id"] = f"{name}@{version}"
        dist = dict(manifest.get("dist") or {})
        dist["integrity"] = _sri_sha512(tarball)
        dist["shasum"] = hashlib.sha1(tarball).hexdigest()
        registry = "https://registry.npmjs.org/" if not self.endpoints.stub else self.endpoints.npm + "/"
        dist["tarball"] = urllib.parse.urljoin(registry, f"{name}/-/{tarball_name}").replace("https://", "http://", 1)
        manifest["dist"] = dist
        document: dict[str, Any] = {
            "_id": name,
            "name": name,
            "dist-tags": {PROBE_DIST_TAG: version},
            "versions": {version: manifest},
            "access": "public",
            "_attachments": {
                tarball_name: {
                    "content_type": "application/octet-stream",
                    "data": base64.b64encode(tarball).decode("ascii"),
                    "length": len(tarball),
                }
            },
        }
        if isinstance(manifest.get("description"), str):
            document["description"] = manifest["description"]
        return document

    # ---- PyPI

    def pypi_rows(self) -> list[Row]:
        return [self.missing_token("pypi", name) or self.pypi_project(name) for name in self.product.pypi]

    def pypi_project(self, name: str) -> Row:
        index = self.read(f"{self.endpoints.pypi_index}/{_normalize_project(name)}/", accept="application/vnd.pypi.simple.v1+json")
        if index.status != 200:
            return self.read_failure("pypi", name, f"the PyPI index page of {name}", index)
        try:
            files = json.loads(index.body)["files"]
            assert isinstance(files, list)
        except (ValueError, KeyError, AssertionError, TypeError):
            return Row("pypi", name, FAIL, status=200, detail="the PyPI index page lists no files")
        wheels: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = {}
        for item in files:
            filename = item.get("filename") if isinstance(item, dict) else None
            if not isinstance(filename, str) or not filename.endswith(".whl") or item.get("yanked"):
                continue
            parts = filename[: -len(".whl")].split("-")
            if len(parts) >= 5 and _normalize_project(parts[0]) == _normalize_project(name):
                wheels.setdefault(parts[1], []).append(item)
        version = choose_version(list(wheels), self.product.excluded_versions)
        if version is None:
            return Row("pypi", name, FAIL, detail=no_version_detail(list(wheels), self.product.excluded_versions))
        wheel = sorted(wheels[version], key=lambda item: item["filename"])[0]
        digest = (wheel.get("hashes") or {}).get("sha256")
        if not isinstance(digest, str) or not isinstance(wheel.get("url"), str):
            return Row("pypi", name, FAIL, version=version, detail="the index records no sha256 or URL for the wheel")
        download = self.read(wheel["url"], accept="application/octet-stream")
        if download.status != 200:
            return self.read_failure("pypi", name, f"the {wheel['filename']} wheel", download, version)
        payload = download.body
        artifact = {"url": wheel["url"], "file": wheel["filename"], "digest": f"sha256:{digest}", "verified": False}
        if hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest() != digest.lower():
            return Row("pypi", name, FAIL, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail="the downloaded wheel does not match PyPI's sha256; nothing was sent")
        if not self.wheel_names(payload, name, version):
            return Row("pypi", name, FAIL, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail="the wheel's METADATA does not name this project and version; nothing was sent")
        artifact["verified"] = True
        request = f"twine upload --repository-url {self.endpoints.pypi_upload} {wheel['filename']} (no --skip-existing)"
        if not self.probe:
            return Row("pypi", name, SKIP, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail=f"plan: would run {request}; published, sha256 verified")
        twine = shutil.which("twine")
        if twine is None:
            return Row("pypi", name, FAIL, version=version, artifact=artifact, detail="twine is not installed")
        workdir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="registry-preflight-pypi-"))
        try:
            path = workdir / wheel["filename"]
            path.write_bytes(payload)
            control = self.twine(twine, path, CONTROL_PASSWORD)
            control_answer = twine_answer(control)
            blocked = self.control_row("pypi", name, version, _twine_response(control), control.returncode == 0,
                                       control_answer, artifact)
            if blocked:
                return blocked
            token = self.tokens["pypi"]
            result, verdict, detail = self.attempt_twine(lambda: self.twine(twine, path, token))
        finally:
            shutil.rmtree(workdir, ignore_errors=True)
        return Row("pypi", name, verdict, version=version, status=twine_status(result) or (200 if result.returncode == 0 else None),
                   answer=self.clip(twine_answer(result)), detail=detail,
                   control={"status": twine_status(control), "answer": self.clip(control_answer)}, artifact=artifact)

    def attempt_twine(self, send: Callable[[], TwineResult]) -> tuple[TwineResult, str, str]:
        result = send()
        verdict, detail = classify_twine(result)
        if verdict == INCONCLUSIVE:
            self.say(f"  inconclusive answer ({twine_answer(result)[:80]}); one retry in {self.args.retry_delay:.0f}s")
            self.sleep(self.args.retry_delay)
            result = send()
            verdict, detail = classify_twine(result)
        return result, verdict, detail

    def twine(self, twine: str, wheel: Path, password: str) -> TwineResult:
        environment = {
            key: value
            for key, value in os.environ.items()
            if key not in TOKEN_ENV.values() and key not in UNSHARED_ENV and not key.startswith("TWINE_")
        }
        environment.update(
            TWINE_USERNAME="__token__",
            TWINE_PASSWORD=password,
            TWINE_NON_INTERACTIVE="1",
            PYTHON_KEYRING_BACKEND="keyring.backends.null.Keyring",
            NO_COLOR="1",
            COLUMNS="400",
        )
        command = [
            twine, "--no-color", "upload", "--non-interactive", "--disable-progress-bar", "--verbose",
            "--repository-url", self.endpoints.pypi_upload, str(wheel),
        ]
        try:
            result = subprocess.run(command, cwd=wheel.parent, env=environment, capture_output=True, text=True,
                                    timeout=600, check=False)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as error:
            return TwineResult(None, "", error=self.secrets.redact(f"{type(error).__name__}: {error}"))
        output = self.secrets.redact((result.stdout or "") + "\n" + (result.stderr or ""))
        return TwineResult(result.returncode, output)

    @staticmethod
    def wheel_names(payload: bytes, name: str, version: str) -> bool:
        try:
            with zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(payload)) as archive:
                metadata = [item for item in archive.namelist() if re.fullmatch(r"[^/]+\.dist-info/METADATA", item)]
                if len(metadata) != 1:
                    return False
                headers = email.parser.BytesHeaderParser().parsebytes(archive.read(metadata[0]))
        except (zipfile.BadZipFile, OSError, KeyError):
            return False
        return _normalize_project(headers.get("Name", "")) == _normalize_project(name) and headers.get("Version") == version

    # ---- crates.io

    def crates_rows(self) -> list[Row]:
        crates = self.product.crates
        if self.args.crates == "all":
            sample = list(crates)
        else:
            sample = [crate for crate in crates if crate in self.product.family_sample]
        rows: dict[str, Row] = {}
        info: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}
        owners: dict[str, set[tuple[str, int]]] = {}
        for crate in crates:
            missing = self.missing_token("crates", crate)
            if missing:
                rows[crate] = missing
                continue
            meta = self.read(f"{self.endpoints.crates_api}/api/v1/crates/{crate}", paced=True)
            if meta.status == 404:
                rows[crate] = Row("crates", crate, FAIL, status=404, answer=self.clip(crates_answer(meta)),
                                  detail="not on crates.io: a first publication needs the publish-new scope (the owner must confirm); no probe can prove it without publishing")
                continue
            if meta.status != 200:
                rows[crate] = self.read_failure("crates", crate, f"the crates.io metadata of {crate}", meta)
                continue
            listed = self.read(f"{self.endpoints.crates_api}/api/v1/crates/{crate}/owners", paced=True)
            try:
                info[crate] = json.loads(meta.body)
                owners[crate] = {
                    (str(user.get("kind")), int(user["id"])) for user in json.loads(listed.body)["users"]
                } if listed.status == 200 else set()
            except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
                rows[crate] = Row("crates", crate, FAIL, status=meta.status, detail="unreadable crates.io metadata or owners")
                continue
            if listed.status != 200:
                rows[crate] = self.read_failure("crates", crate, f"the owners of {crate}", listed)
                continue
            if (info[crate].get("crate") or {}).get("trustpub_only") is True:
                rows[crate] = Row("crates", crate, FAIL,
                                  detail="trusted-publishing-only: crates.io refuses every token publish of it")
        probed = [crate for crate in sample if crate not in rows]
        baseline = set.intersection(*(owners[crate] for crate in probed)) if probed else set()
        delays = probe_delays(len(probed), self.args.crates_burst if self.args.crates == "all" else len(probed),
                              self.args.crates_interval)
        for crate, delay in zip(probed, delays):
            if self.probe and delay:
                self.say(f"crates.io: pacing to the publish rate limit, next probe in {delay:.0f}s")
                self.sleep(delay)
            rows[crate] = self.crate_probe(crate, info[crate])
        for crate in crates:
            if crate in rows:
                continue
            if not baseline:
                rows[crate] = Row("crates", crate, FAIL, detail=(
                    "no family sample crate could be checked, so nothing vouches for it"))
            elif not baseline <= owners[crate]:
                rows[crate] = Row("crates", crate, FAIL, detail=(
                    "its owners do not include every owner of the probed crates, so the family probe cannot vouch for it: "
                    "run --crates all"))
            else:
                rows[crate] = Row("crates", crate, SKIP, detail=(
                    "not probed (family sample); it exists, is not trusted-publishing-only and its owners include the probed crates' owners"))
        return [rows[crate] for crate in crates]

    def crate_probe(self, crate: str, info: dict[str, Any]) -> Row:
        if not isinstance(info.get("versions"), list):
            return Row("crates", crate, FAIL, detail="the crates.io metadata carries no version list")
        versions = [item for item in info.get("versions") or [] if isinstance(item, dict) and not item.get("yanked")]
        by_number = {str(item.get("num")): item for item in versions}
        version = choose_version(list(by_number), self.product.excluded_versions)
        if version is None:
            return Row("crates", crate, FAIL, detail=no_version_detail(list(by_number), self.product.excluded_versions))
        checksum = by_number[version].get("checksum")
        if not isinstance(checksum, str) or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{64}", checksum):
            return Row("crates", crate, FAIL, version=version, detail="crates.io records no checksum for this version")
        url = f"{self.endpoints.crates_static}/crates/{crate}/{crate}-{version}.crate"
        download = self.read(url, accept="application/octet-stream")
        if download.status != 200:
            return self.read_failure("crates", crate, f"{crate}-{version}.crate", download, version)
        payload = download.body
        artifact = {"url": url, "digest": f"sha256:{checksum}", "verified": False}
        if hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest() != checksum:
            return Row("crates", crate, FAIL, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail="the downloaded .crate does not match the crates.io checksum; nothing was sent")
        try:
            package = tomllib.loads(_text(_tar_member(payload, f"{crate}-{version}/Cargo.toml") or b"")).get("package", {})
        except tomllib.TOMLDecodeError:
            package = {}
        if package.get("name") != crate or package.get("version") != version:
            return Row("crates", crate, FAIL, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail="the .crate's Cargo.toml does not name this crate and version; nothing was sent")
        artifact["verified"] = True
        url = f"{self.endpoints.crates_api}/api/v1/crates/new"
        if not self.probe:
            return Row("crates", crate, SKIP, version=version, artifact=artifact,
                       detail=f"plan: would send PUT {url} with the published {crate}-{version}.crate; published, checksum verified")
        metadata = json.dumps({"name": crate, "vers": version}).encode()
        body = struct.pack("<I", len(metadata)) + metadata + struct.pack("<I", len(payload)) + payload
        headers = {"Content-Type": "application/octet-stream", "Accept": "application/json"}
        control = http("PUT", url, headers=headers, body=body, credentials=True)
        blocked = self.control_row("crates", crate, version, control, crates_is_duplicate(control, version),
                                   crates_answer(control), artifact)
        if blocked:
            return blocked
        token = self.tokens["crates"]
        response, verdict, detail = self.attempt(
            lambda: http("PUT", url, headers={**headers, "Authorization": token}, body=body, credentials=True),
            lambda answer: classify_crates(answer, version),
        )
        return Row("crates", crate, verdict, version=version, status=response.status, answer=self.clip(crates_answer(response)),
                   detail=detail, control={"status": control.status, "answer": self.clip(crates_answer(control))}, artifact=artifact)


def _twine_response(result: TwineResult) -> Response:
    """A twine run as a Response, for the control check."""
    status = twine_status(result)
    if result.returncode == 0:
        status = status or 200
    return Response(status, {}, b"", error=result.error)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Command line.


def resolve_endpoints() -> Endpoints:
    stub = os.environ.get(STUB_ENV, "").strip()
    if not stub:
        return Endpoints(
            npm="https://registry.npmjs.org",
            pypi_index="https://pypi.org/simple",
            pypi_upload="https://upload.pypi.org/legacy/",
            crates_api="https://crates.io",
            crates_static="https://static.crates.io",
            stub=False,
        )
    parsed = urllib.parse.urlsplit(stub)
    if parsed.scheme not in ("http", "https") or parsed.hostname not in ("127.0.0.1", "localhost", "::1"):
        raise UsageError(f"{STUB_ENV} must be a loopback URL (the self-test's stub); tokens never go elsewhere")
    base = stub.rstrip("/")
    return Endpoints(
        npm=f"{base}/npm",
        pypi_index=f"{base}/pypi/simple",
        pypi_upload=f"{base}/pypi/legacy/",
        crates_api=f"{base}/crates",
        crates_static=f"{base}/static",
        stub=True,
    )


def parse_args(argv: list[str] | None) -> argparse.Namespace:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    parser.add_argument("--product", required=True, choices=sorted(PRODUCTS))
    parser.add_argument("--mode", choices=("plan", "probe"), default="plan",
                        help="plan (default): read, check and print, write nothing; probe: send the probes")
    parser.add_argument("--registry", default=",".join(REGISTRIES),
                        help="comma-separated subset of npm,pypi,crates (default: all three)")
    parser.add_argument("--crates", choices=("family", "all"), default="family",
                        help="family (default): the fixed crates.io sample; all: every crate, paced (early run only)")
    parser.add_argument("--release-version", default=None, help="a version never probed (the release's)")
    parser.add_argument("--report", type=Path, default=None, help="write the JSON report here")
    parser.add_argument("--repo-root", type=Path, default=REPO_ROOT)
    parser.add_argument("--crates-burst", type=int, default=20,
                        help=f"--crates all: probes sent back to back before pacing (at most {CRATES_BURST_LIMIT})")
    parser.add_argument("--crates-interval", type=float, default=61.0,
                        help=f"--crates all: seconds between paced probes (at least {CRATES_MIN_INTERVAL})")
    parser.add_argument("--retry-delay", type=float, default=10.0,
                        help="seconds before the one retry of an inconclusive answer (429 waits its Retry-After)")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    registries = [item.strip() for item in args.registry.split(",") if item.strip()]
    unknown = sorted(set(registries) - set(REGISTRIES))
    if unknown or not registries or len(set(registries)) != len(registries):
        parser.error(f"--registry takes a subset of {','.join(REGISTRIES)}, got {args.registry!r}")
    args.registries = [registry for registry in REGISTRIES if registry in registries]
    if not 1 <= args.crates_burst <= CRATES_BURST_LIMIT:
        parser.error(f"--crates-burst must be 1..{CRATES_BURST_LIMIT}: the crates.io publish burst is {CRATES_BURST_LIMIT}")
    if args.crates_interval < CRATES_MIN_INTERVAL:
        parser.error(f"--crates-interval must be at least {CRATES_MIN_INTERVAL}: crates.io refills one publish token a minute")
    if args.retry_delay < 0:
        parser.error("--retry-delay must not be negative")
    return args


def summary_markdown(product: Product, args: argparse.Namespace, rows: list[Row]) -> str:
    def cell(text: str) -> str:
        return text.replace("|", "\\|").replace("\n", " ")

    lines = [
        f"### Registry pre-flight: {product.name} ({args.mode}, crates {args.crates})",
        "",
        "| Verdict | Registry | Package | Version | HTTP | Registry answer | Conclusion |",
        "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |",
    ]
    for row in rows:
        lines.append(
            f"| {row.verdict} | {row.registry} | {cell(row.package)} | {row.version or '-'} | "
            f"{row.status if row.status is not None else '-'} | {cell(row.answer) or '-'} | {cell(row.detail)} |"
        )
    return "\n".join(lines) + "\n"


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    args = parse_args(argv)
    try:
        endpoints = resolve_endpoints()
        if args.crates == "all" and RELEASE_WORKFLOWS.search(os.environ.get("GITHUB_WORKFLOW_REF", "")):
            raise UsageError(
                "--crates all spends a crates.io publish token per crate; it runs only in the early "
                "registry-preflight.yml dispatch, never inside a release workflow"
            )
        product = load_product(args.repo_root.resolve(), args.product, args.release_version)
        if args.crates == "family" and "crates" in args.registries:
            stale = [crate for crate in product.family_sample if crate not in product.crates]
            if stale:
                raise UsageError(
                    f"the {product.name} family sample names {stale}, which its crate list does not: "
                    "update PRODUCTS' family_sample"
                )
    except UsageError as error:
        print(f"release-registry-preflight: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    run = Run(args, endpoints, product)
    sample = list(product.crates) if args.crates == "all" else [c for c in product.crates if c in product.family_sample]
    run.say(f"registry pre-flight: product {product.name}, mode {args.mode}, registries {','.join(args.registries)}")
    run.say(f"  never probed (release versions): {', '.join(sorted(product.excluded_versions))}")
    if "crates" in args.registries:
        run.say(
            f"  crates.io: {len(product.crates)} crates, {args.crates} probe of {len(sample)} "
            f"({len(sample)} publish-rate tokens): {', '.join(sample)}"
        )
    if args.mode == "plan":
        run.say("  plan mode: every read and check, no write, no token")

    rows: list[Row] = []
    for registry in args.registries:
        rows.extend({"npm": run.npm_rows, "pypi": run.pypi_rows, "crates": run.crates_rows}[registry]())

    counts = {verdict: sum(1 for row in rows if row.verdict == verdict) for verdict in (PASS, FAIL, INCONCLUSIVE, SKIP)}
    for row in rows:
        status = f"HTTP {row.status}" if row.status is not None else "-"
        answer = f' "{row.answer}"' if row.answer else ""
        run.say(f"{row.verdict:<12} {row.registry:<6} {row.package} {row.version or '-'}: {status}{answer} ({row.detail})")
    ok = counts[FAIL] == 0 and counts[INCONCLUSIVE] == 0 and (args.mode == "plan" or counts[PASS] > 0)
    run.say(
        f"registry pre-flight {product.name}: {counts[PASS]} PASS, {counts[FAIL]} FAIL, "
        f"{counts[INCONCLUSIVE]} INCONCLUSIVE, {counts[SKIP]} SKIP: {'ok' if ok else 'NOT OK'}"
    )
    if args.mode == "probe" and counts[PASS] == 0 and counts[FAIL] == 0 and counts[INCONCLUSIVE] == 0:
        run.say("refusing a probe that proved no package")

    report = {
        "schema_version": 1,
        "product": product.name,
        "mode": args.mode,
        "registries": args.registries,
        "crates": args.crates,
        "crates_sample": sample if "crates" in args.registries else [],
        "never_probed_versions": sorted(product.excluded_versions),
        "generated_at": datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"),
        "ok": ok,
        "counts": counts,
        "packages": [dataclasses.asdict(row) for row in rows],
    }
    text = run.secrets.redact(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + "\n")
    if args.report:
        args.report.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        args.report.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8")
    step_summary = os.environ.get("GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY")
    if step_summary:
        with open(step_summary, "a", encoding="utf-8") as handle:
            handle.write(run.secrets.redact(summary_markdown(product, args, rows)))
    return 0 if ok else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
